# Simplified Technical English

Use ASD-STE100 Simplified Technical English for text in this project and for replies about this project.

- Write short sentences. Use one subject and one action in each sentence.
- Use the active voice.
- Use the same word for the same thing. Do not use a synonym.
- Use concrete words. Do not use slang, idioms, or metaphors.
- Put one instruction in each step.
- Keep procedure steps in the correct order.
- If a sentence is longer than 20 words, split it.

Product names stay as written: Questodoro, HOW YA, GRINDING, PUSH.
